  "segment": {
    "id": "s03",
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "So you send a comment, and the server takes a few seconds. Normally you write extra code just to track the waiting and stop the reload. useActionState gives you the saved comments, a submit function and a waiting flag, all in one line. So whenever a form has a slow save, that's what you reach for. We'll look at the old way, how it works, and how to build it, and then we'll try two clicks at once, a failure and a reset.",
